--- a/docs/gmap-workflow.qmd
+++ b/docs/gmap-workflow.qmd
@@ -18,6 +18,56 @@ This example requires development installations of gbase, gbayes, gmap and gsim.
 The website displays saved results and does not run models. The current calls
 are shown below; a refreshed end-to-end script remains separate work.
 
+## Familiar summary-statistic calls
+
+For statistics computed from the selected BED people, regional BayesC/BayesR
+can use full LD directly in memory:
+
+```r
+G <- gbase::gprep(bedfiles="cohort.bed")
+sets <- list(locus=c("marker1", "marker2", "marker3"))
+fit <- gmap::gmap(Glist=G, stat=stat, sets=sets, method="bayesC",
+  algorithm="mcmc", nit=1000, nburn=100, seed=10, output="full")
+head(fit$stat)       # bm: native posterior effect mean; dm: PIP
+fit$post            # native parameter summaries
+fit$conv            # native regional diagnostics
+fit$cs              # marginal-PIP/LD groups by region
+fit$timings         # decoding, LD product, preparation and sampling phases
+```
+
+`gbase::mapSets(sets, Glist=G)` maps named marker sets to prepared marker IDs or indices;
+unknown members are dropped and empty sets stay visible. `gbase::getLD(G,
+rsids=sets$locus)` returns full regional correlation in requested marker order
+without writing an LD file. Missing dosages are mean-imputed. Local `nthreads`
+controls decoding; the dense product uses R's configured BLAS.
+
+`algorithm="mcmc"` requires positive-definite LD, applies no PSD repair or
+truncation, and does not require sparse LD. `algorithm="mcmc-eigen"` retains
+the sparse-LD eigen route and its explicit retained-mass controls. Existing
+`regions` and score/information calls retain their advanced defaults.
+
+Familiar calls default to one chain, 1000 post-burn sweeps, 100 burn-in sweeps,
+`h2=.5`, `mc=5000`, BayesC weights `c(.99,.01)`, and learned slab/residual
+variances and mixture weights. Residual learning asserts in-sample LD and
+rejects a likelihood dimension exceeding the selected reference sample count.
+`nit`, `nburn`, `nthin`, `nrun`, `seed`, `pi`, `gamma`, `vb`, `ve` and
+`updateB/updateE/updatePi` adapt to native controls; conflicting explicit aliases
+and nested settings are rejected. No independent genetic-variance draw is
+added. `post` and `conv` retain native columns and meanings. One-chain fits
+remain provisional.
+
+Saved regional or genome-wide PIPs can be grouped without refitting:
+
+```r
+groups <- gmap::getCredibleSets(Glist=G, fit=fit, sets=sets,
+  cs_threshold=.8, cs_r2=.5, cs_method="CS2")
+```
+
+This standalone native helper reproduces qgg CS2/CS3 ordering and strict
+`LD^2 > r2` neighborhoods. Its grouping target is marginal-PIP mass (expected
+active-marker count), not guaranteed component credible coverage. It has no
+qgg runtime dependency. Multi-trait results require an explicit `trait`.
+
